{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/upstash/agentkit/tree/main/packages/tanstack-ai","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nimplements TanStack AI's state contracts on "},{"type":"link","href":"https://upstash.com/docs/redis/overall/getstarted","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upstash Redis"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nThe built-in implementations ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStream()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InMemoryLockStore"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":") live in one process. These keep the same state in Redis, so every serverless\ninstance sees it. The client is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@upstash/redis"},{"type":"text","value":", which talks HTTP, so it works on edge and\nserverless runtimes without a connection pool."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI seam"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upstash adapter"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withGenerationPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" stores"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashPersistence()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamDurability"},{"type":"text","value":" for resumable streams"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashStream()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LockStore"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withLocks()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashLocks()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MemoryAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashMemory()"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runPersistenceConformance"},{"type":"text","value":" with all seven stores, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runMemoryAdapterContract"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai\",\"@tanstack/ai\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence and memory have their own entry points, so install the TanStack package for the\nones you use: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-memory"},{"type":"text","value":" for\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/memory"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every factory reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN"},{"type":"text","value":", or takes a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis"},{"type":"text","value":" client:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io\nUPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-token","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runs"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" stores, plus\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generationRuns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"artifacts"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" as you would any adapter:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { upstashPersistence } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence'\n\nconst persistence = upstashPersistence()\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Records are RedisJSON documents. Runs and interrupts are listed through sorted-set indexes\n(per thread, per run, per parent run, and by detach time for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listReclaimable"},{"type":"text","value":"), and each\nwrite updates the document and its indexes in one Lua script, so two instances cannot\ninterleave a write. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOrResume"},{"type":"text","value":" is insert-if-absent and interrupt "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commitBatch"},{"type":"text","value":" is\nall-or-nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reconstructChat(persistence, request, …)"},{"type":"text","value":" works unchanged, so the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" handler from the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":" needs no other edits."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To keep generated files, pass an "},{"type":"link","href":"https://upstash.com/docs/blob","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upstash Blob"}]},{"type":"text","value":" bucket. It\nadds a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":" store: bytes go to the bucket, records to Redis, and ranged reads use HTTP\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Range"},{"type":"text","value":" requests."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Bucket } from '@upstash/blob'\nimport { upstashPersistence } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence'\n\nconst persistence = upstashPersistence({ bucket: Bucket.fromEnv() })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Redis.fromEnv()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@upstash/redis"},{"type":"text","value":" client."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prefix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'agentkit:tanstack'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key namespace."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messagesTtlSeconds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expire idle transcripts. Runs, interrupts, and metadata never expire."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bucket"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"none"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upstash Blob bucket for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blobs"},{"type":"text","value":" store."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"resumable-streams","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resumable streams"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashStream(request)"},{"type":"text","value":" is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamDurability"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter. Every chunk is appended to a Redis\nStream before it is delivered, and a client that reconnects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Last-Event-ID"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"?offset="},{"type":"text","value":" replays what it missed and keeps tailing the live run, on any instance."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashStream } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, {\n    durability: { adapter: upstashStream(request) },\n  })\n}\n\nexport function GET(request: Request) {\n  return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: upstashStream(request) })\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outside a request handler, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashStream({ runId, offset })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ttlSeconds"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"86400"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How long a run stays resumable after its last chunk."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pollIntervalMs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"150"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tail poll interval. The REST API has no blocking reads."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"firstChunkDeadlineMs"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2000"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How long a from-start reader waits for a run that has not produced yet."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"locks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashLocks()"},{"type":"text","value":" is a distributed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LockStore"},{"type":"text","value":". Hand it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withLocks"},{"type":"text","value":" in place of\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InMemoryLockStore"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":" (or your own middleware, through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getLocks"},{"type":"text","value":") takes\nthe lock across instances:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withLocks } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashLocks } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai'\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  middleware: [withLocks(upstashLocks())],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each lock is a lease ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"leaseMs"},{"type":"text","value":", default 30 seconds) that is renewed while "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fn"},{"type":"text","value":" runs. If\nrenewal fails, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"},{"type":"text","value":" passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fn"},{"type":"text","value":" aborts, as the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/locks#distributed-locks-and-leases","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lock contract"}]},{"type":"text","value":" requires. Release and\nrenewal check ownership in Lua, so an expired owner cannot release a lock someone else now\nholds."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"memory","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"upstashMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MemoryAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" backed by Upstash Redis Search. Recall is a BM25\nfull-text query in Redis, so it does not scan every record on each turn."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashMemory } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/memory'\n\ndeclare const session: { userId: string }\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: upstashMemory(),\n      // Derive the user from your session, never from the request body.\n      scope: (ctx) => ({ threadId: ctx.threadId, userId: session.userId }),\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory is per user across threads by default, or per thread when the scope has no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"userId"},{"type":"text","value":".\nSet "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scopeBy: 'thread'"},{"type":"text","value":" to keep it per conversation. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tenantId"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"namespace"},{"type":"text","value":" always\npartition."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Purpose"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scopeBy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'user'"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Share memories across a user's threads, or keep them per "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'thread'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"saveTool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the model a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save_memory"},{"type":"text","value":" tool for durable facts."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"captureUserMessages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store each turn's user message."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitForIndexing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for the index on save, so a memory is recallable on the next turn."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"also-in-the-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Also in the package"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolCache()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rateLimit()"},{"type":"text","value":": chat middleware that serves repeated tool calls from Redis\nand limits runs per user before the model is called."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSearchTools()"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"search"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregate"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"count"},{"type":"text","value":" tools over your own documents."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://upstash.com/docs/redis/sdks/agentkit/tanstack-ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AgentKit for TanStack AI docs"}]},{"type":"text","value":": every option and feature"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/upstash/agentkit/tree/main/packages/tanstack-ai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"GitHub repository"}]},{"type":"text","value":": source and issues"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Persistence Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the server and client halves"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../resumable-streams/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resumable Streams"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the delivery layer"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/locks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locks"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LockStore"},{"type":"text","value":" contract"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../memory/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Memory"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" contract"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"persistence","text":"Persistence","level":2},{"id":"resumable-streams","text":"Resumable streams","level":2},{"id":"locks","text":"Locks","level":2},{"id":"memory","text":"Memory","level":2},{"id":"also-in-the-package","text":"Also in the package","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\n[`@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai`](https://github.com/upstash/agentkit/tree/main/packages/tanstack-ai)\nimplements TanStack AI's state contracts on [Upstash Redis](https://upstash.com/docs/redis/overall/getstarted).\nThe built-in implementations (`memoryPersistence()`, `memoryStream()`, `InMemoryLockStore`,\n`inMemory()`) live in one process. These keep the same state in Redis, so every serverless\ninstance sees it. The client is `@upstash/redis`, which talks HTTP, so it works on edge and\nserverless runtimes without a connection pool.\n\n| TanStack AI seam | Upstash adapter |\n| --- | --- |\n| `withPersistence()` / `withGenerationPersistence()` stores | `upstashPersistence()` |\n| `StreamDurability` for resumable streams | `upstashStream()` |\n| `LockStore` for `withLocks()` | `upstashLocks()` |\n| `MemoryAdapter` for `memoryMiddleware()` | `upstashMemory()` |\n\n`upstashPersistence()` passes `runPersistenceConformance` with all seven stores, and\n`upstashMemory()` passes `runMemoryAdapterContract`.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nvue: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\npreact: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nangular: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\noctane: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPersistence and memory have their own entry points, so install the TanStack package for the\nones you use: `@tanstack/ai-persistence` for `/persistence` and `@tanstack/ai-memory` for\n`/memory`.\n\nEvery factory reads `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` and `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`, or takes a\n`redis` client:\n\n```bash\nUPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io\nUPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-token\n```\n\n## Persistence\n\n`upstashPersistence()` returns the `messages`, `runs`, `interrupts`, and `metadata` stores, plus\n`generationRuns` and `artifacts`. Pass it to `withPersistence` as you would any adapter:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { upstashPersistence } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence'\n\nconst persistence = upstashPersistence()\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n})\n```\n\nRecords are RedisJSON documents. Runs and interrupts are listed through sorted-set indexes\n(per thread, per run, per parent run, and by detach time for `listReclaimable`), and each\nwrite updates the document and its indexes in one Lua script, so two instances cannot\ninterleave a write. `createOrResume` is insert-if-absent and interrupt `commitBatch` is\nall-or-nothing.\n\n`reconstructChat(persistence, request, …)` works unchanged, so the `GET` handler from the\n[Persistence Overview](../persistence/overview) needs no other edits.\n\nTo keep generated files, pass an [Upstash Blob](https://upstash.com/docs/blob) bucket. It\nadds a `blobs` store: bytes go to the bucket, records to Redis, and ranged reads use HTTP\n`Range` requests.\n\n```ts\nimport { Bucket } from '@upstash/blob'\nimport { upstashPersistence } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence'\n\nconst persistence = upstashPersistence({ bucket: Bucket.fromEnv() })\n```\n\n| Option | Default | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `redis` | `Redis.fromEnv()` | Your `@upstash/redis` client. |\n| `prefix` | `'agentkit:tanstack'` | Key namespace. |\n| `messagesTtlSeconds` | none | Expire idle transcripts. Runs, interrupts, and metadata never expire. |\n| `bucket` | none | Upstash Blob bucket for the `blobs` store. |\n\n## Resumable streams\n\n`upstashStream(request)` is a `StreamDurability` adapter. Every chunk is appended to a Redis\nStream before it is delivered, and a client that reconnects with `Last-Event-ID` or\n`?offset=` replays what it missed and keeps tailing the live run, on any instance.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashStream } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, {\n    durability: { adapter: upstashStream(request) },\n  })\n}\n\nexport function GET(request: Request) {\n  return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: upstashStream(request) })\n}\n```\n\nOutside a request handler, use `upstashStream({ runId, offset })`.\n\n| Option | Default | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `ttlSeconds` | `86400` | How long a run stays resumable after its last chunk. |\n| `pollIntervalMs` | `150` | Tail poll interval. The REST API has no blocking reads. |\n| `firstChunkDeadlineMs` | `2000` | How long a from-start reader waits for a run that has not produced yet. |\n\n## Locks\n\n`upstashLocks()` is a distributed `LockStore`. Hand it to `withLocks` in place of\n`InMemoryLockStore`, and `withSandbox` (or your own middleware, through `getLocks`) takes\nthe lock across instances:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withLocks } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashLocks } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai'\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  middleware: [withLocks(upstashLocks())],\n})\n```\n\nEach lock is a lease (`leaseMs`, default 30 seconds) that is renewed while `fn` runs. If\nrenewal fails, the `signal` passed to `fn` aborts, as the\n[lock contract](../advanced/locks#distributed-locks-and-leases) requires. Release and\nrenewal check ownership in Lua, so an expired owner cannot release a lock someone else now\nholds.\n\n## Memory\n\n`upstashMemory()` is a `MemoryAdapter` backed by Upstash Redis Search. Recall is a BM25\nfull-text query in Redis, so it does not scan every record on each turn.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashMemory } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/memory'\n\ndeclare const session: { userId: string }\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: upstashMemory(),\n      // Derive the user from your session, never from the request body.\n      scope: (ctx) => ({ threadId: ctx.threadId, userId: session.userId }),\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nMemory is per user across threads by default, or per thread when the scope has no `userId`.\nSet `scopeBy: 'thread'` to keep it per conversation. `tenantId` and `namespace` always\npartition.\n\n| Option | Default | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `scopeBy` | `'user'` | Share memories across a user's threads, or keep them per `'thread'`. |\n| `saveTool` | `true` | Give the model a `save_memory` tool for durable facts. |\n| `captureUserMessages` | `true` | Store each turn's user message. |\n| `waitForIndexing` | `true` | Wait for the index on save, so a memory is recallable on the next turn. |\n\n## Also in the package\n\n- `toolCache()` and `rateLimit()`: chat middleware that serves repeated tool calls from Redis\n  and limits runs per user before the model is called.\n- `createSearchTools()`: `search`, `aggregate`, and `count` tools over your own documents.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [AgentKit for TanStack AI docs](https://upstash.com/docs/redis/sdks/agentkit/tanstack-ai): every option and feature\n- [GitHub repository](https://github.com/upstash/agentkit/tree/main/packages/tanstack-ai): source and issues\n- [Persistence Overview](../persistence/overview): the server and client halves\n- [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview): the delivery layer\n- [Locks](../advanced/locks): the `LockStore` contract\n- [Memory](../memory/overview): the `recall`/`save` contract\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Upstash\nid: upstash-adapter\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Back TanStack AI persistence, resumable streams, locks, and memory with Upstash Redis, so they hold across serverless instances, reloads, and devices.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - upstash\n  - redis\n  - persistence\n  - resumable streams\n  - locks\n  - memory\n  - serverless\n  - community adapter\n---\n\n[`@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai`](https://github.com/upstash/agentkit/tree/main/packages/tanstack-ai)\nimplements TanStack AI's state contracts on [Upstash Redis](https://upstash.com/docs/redis/overall/getstarted).\nThe built-in implementations (`memoryPersistence()`, `memoryStream()`, `InMemoryLockStore`,\n`inMemory()`) live in one process. These keep the same state in Redis, so every serverless\ninstance sees it. The client is `@upstash/redis`, which talks HTTP, so it works on edge and\nserverless runtimes without a connection pool.\n\n| TanStack AI seam | Upstash adapter |\n| --- | --- |\n| `withPersistence()` / `withGenerationPersistence()` stores | `upstashPersistence()` |\n| `StreamDurability` for resumable streams | `upstashStream()` |\n| `LockStore` for `withLocks()` | `upstashLocks()` |\n| `MemoryAdapter` for `memoryMiddleware()` | `upstashMemory()` |\n\n`upstashPersistence()` passes `runPersistenceConformance` with all seven stores, and\n`upstashMemory()` passes `runMemoryAdapterContract`.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nvue: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\npreact: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nangular: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\noctane: @upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPersistence and memory have their own entry points, so install the TanStack package for the\nones you use: `@tanstack/ai-persistence` for `/persistence` and `@tanstack/ai-memory` for\n`/memory`.\n\nEvery factory reads `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL` and `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`, or takes a\n`redis` client:\n\n```bash\nUPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io\nUPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-token\n```\n\n## Persistence\n\n`upstashPersistence()` returns the `messages`, `runs`, `interrupts`, and `metadata` stores, plus\n`generationRuns` and `artifacts`. Pass it to `withPersistence` as you would any adapter:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { upstashPersistence } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence'\n\nconst persistence = upstashPersistence()\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n})\n```\n\nRecords are RedisJSON documents. Runs and interrupts are listed through sorted-set indexes\n(per thread, per run, per parent run, and by detach time for `listReclaimable`), and each\nwrite updates the document and its indexes in one Lua script, so two instances cannot\ninterleave a write. `createOrResume` is insert-if-absent and interrupt `commitBatch` is\nall-or-nothing.\n\n`reconstructChat(persistence, request, …)` works unchanged, so the `GET` handler from the\n[Persistence Overview](../persistence/overview) needs no other edits.\n\nTo keep generated files, pass an [Upstash Blob](https://upstash.com/docs/blob) bucket. It\nadds a `blobs` store: bytes go to the bucket, records to Redis, and ranged reads use HTTP\n`Range` requests.\n\n```ts\nimport { Bucket } from '@upstash/blob'\nimport { upstashPersistence } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/persistence'\n\nconst persistence = upstashPersistence({ bucket: Bucket.fromEnv() })\n```\n\n| Option | Default | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `redis` | `Redis.fromEnv()` | Your `@upstash/redis` client. |\n| `prefix` | `'agentkit:tanstack'` | Key namespace. |\n| `messagesTtlSeconds` | none | Expire idle transcripts. Runs, interrupts, and metadata never expire. |\n| `bucket` | none | Upstash Blob bucket for the `blobs` store. |\n\n## Resumable streams\n\n`upstashStream(request)` is a `StreamDurability` adapter. Every chunk is appended to a Redis\nStream before it is delivered, and a client that reconnects with `Last-Event-ID` or\n`?offset=` replays what it missed and keeps tailing the live run, on any instance.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashStream } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, {\n    durability: { adapter: upstashStream(request) },\n  })\n}\n\nexport function GET(request: Request) {\n  return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: upstashStream(request) })\n}\n```\n\nOutside a request handler, use `upstashStream({ runId, offset })`.\n\n| Option | Default | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `ttlSeconds` | `86400` | How long a run stays resumable after its last chunk. |\n| `pollIntervalMs` | `150` | Tail poll interval. The REST API has no blocking reads. |\n| `firstChunkDeadlineMs` | `2000` | How long a from-start reader waits for a run that has not produced yet. |\n\n## Locks\n\n`upstashLocks()` is a distributed `LockStore`. Hand it to `withLocks` in place of\n`InMemoryLockStore`, and `withSandbox` (or your own middleware, through `getLocks`) takes\nthe lock across instances:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { withLocks } from '@tanstack/ai/locks'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashLocks } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai'\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  middleware: [withLocks(upstashLocks())],\n})\n```\n\nEach lock is a lease (`leaseMs`, default 30 seconds) that is renewed while `fn` runs. If\nrenewal fails, the `signal` passed to `fn` aborts, as the\n[lock contract](../advanced/locks#distributed-locks-and-leases) requires. Release and\nrenewal check ownership in Lua, so an expired owner cannot release a lock someone else now\nholds.\n\n## Memory\n\n`upstashMemory()` is a `MemoryAdapter` backed by Upstash Redis Search. Recall is a BM25\nfull-text query in Redis, so it does not scan every record on each turn.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { upstashMemory } from '@upstash/agentkit-tanstack-ai/memory'\n\ndeclare const session: { userId: string }\n\nexport const stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'hi' }],\n  threadId: 'support-chat',\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: upstashMemory(),\n      // Derive the user from your session, never from the request body.\n      scope: (ctx) => ({ threadId: ctx.threadId, userId: session.userId }),\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nMemory is per user across threads by default, or per thread when the scope has no `userId`.\nSet `scopeBy: 'thread'` to keep it per conversation. `tenantId` and `namespace` always\npartition.\n\n| Option | Default | Purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `scopeBy` | `'user'` | Share memories across a user's threads, or keep them per `'thread'`. |\n| `saveTool` | `true` | Give the model a `save_memory` tool for durable facts. |\n| `captureUserMessages` | `true` | Store each turn's user message. |\n| `waitForIndexing` | `true` | Wait for the index on save, so a memory is recallable on the next turn. |\n\n## Also in the package\n\n- `toolCache()` and `rateLimit()`: chat middleware that serves repeated tool calls from Redis\n  and limits runs per user before the model is called.\n- `createSearchTools()`: `search`, `aggregate`, and `count` tools over your own documents.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [AgentKit for TanStack AI docs](https://upstash.com/docs/redis/sdks/agentkit/tanstack-ai): every option and feature\n- [GitHub repository](https://github.com/upstash/agentkit/tree/main/packages/tanstack-ai): source and issues\n- [Persistence Overview](../persistence/overview): the server and client halves\n- [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview): the delivery layer\n- [Locks](../advanced/locks): the `LockStore` contract\n- [Memory](../memory/overview): the `recall`/`save` contract\n"}
